From: AbelDuan <32724782+AbelDuan@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 19:10:23 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 30/31] perf(config): stop waking the manager from every hooked
 app

The system app-policy page reported 146 background wake-ups for the module
in 13 hours, mostly broadcast/notification. Every poll of every hooked app
called requestConfigSync(), which broadcast an ordered intent to the
manager's ConfigRequestReceiver; startup also probed its SettingsProvider.
Each request started the manager process, the system froze it again, and
the next poll repeated the cycle.

Configuration only needs one direction: LocalSettings.publishConfig sends
the bundle to every running target when the user saves, and a target
reads the exported preferences on cold start. Targets now answer sync
requests from memory, the startup path and the per-poll read no longer
probe the provider, and the extra CONFIG_REQUEST broadcast on host attach
is gone. The manager is no longer started by its own hook clients.
